.TH CREATE-CLASTER.SH 1 "2026-09-09" "pg_claster_creator 2.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
create-claster.sh \- prepare PostgreSQL packages and manage PostgreSQL clusters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B create-claster.sh
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B create-claster.sh
.B --action
.I action
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ version " " cluster ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B create-claster.sh
is an interactive and non-interactive administration utility for PostgreSQL,
Postgres Pro Enterprise, and Tantor Free on APT-based Linux systems.
It verifies required packages, prepares the service filesystem, and manages
cluster installation, ports, data placement, backups, restores, databases,
roles, and deletion.
.PP
Without
.BR --action ,
the program opens an interactive menu. Supplying an action or its matching
.B PGCC_ACTION
environment variable disables prompts and requires all action-specific values.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B info
In interactive mode, display a numbered list of registered clusters. After an
online cluster is selected, display a numbered list of all its databases,
including templates, and the size of each database. The selected cluster data
directory size is shown as well. Human-readable sizes use two fractional digits,
a two-letter unit, and an aligned field no longer than nine characters. A
stopped cluster is not started automatically.
Non-interactive mode prints the
.BR pg_lsclusters (1)
table without prompting for a selection.
.TP
.B install
Create a cluster, database, schema, application roles, and systemd unit. If the
requested port is occupied, non-interactive mode selects the next free port and
prints a warning with a command for changing it later. Interactive mode prompts
for another value.
.TP
.B port
Change the TCP port of an existing cluster.
.TP
.B move-data
Move a cluster data directory to the default placement or to
.IR ROOT/pg_VERSION/CLUSTER .
.TP
.B backup
Create a cold cluster archive or a hot custom-format database dump.
.TP
.B restore
Restore a cold cluster archive or a hot database dump.
.TP
.B delete
Delete a cluster. Interactive mode can also delete one database. Before
deletion, the menu always offers a cold cluster backup or a hot backup of the
selected database. Declining a backup requires separate confirmation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print complete usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR -v , " --version"
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.BI "-a, --action " ACTION
Select a non-interactive action.
.TP
.BI "--package " PACKAGE
Select an exact PostgreSQL server package.
.TP
.BI "--pg-family " FAMILY
Select
.BR postgresql ,
.BR postgrespro-ent ,
or
.BR tantor-free .
.TP
.BI "--pg-version " VERSION
Set the PostgreSQL major version.
.TP
.BI "--cluster-name " NAME
Set the source, target, or new cluster name.
.TP
.BI "--port " PORT
Set the cluster TCP port.
.TP
.BI "--schema " NAME
Set the application schema and owner role.
.TP
.BI "--user " NAME
Set the application login role.
.TP
.BI "--password " PASSWORD
Set the application role password.
.TP
.BI "--data-root " DIRECTORY
Select a custom root for cluster installation or data movement. Missing root
and pg_VERSION directories are created when deployment or movement starts.
.TP
.BI "--backup-dir " DIRECTORY
Select backup storage and search directory.
.TP
.BI "--backup-file " FILE
Select a relative or absolute archive for restore.
.TP
.BI "--backup-type " TYPE
Select
.B hot
or
.B cold;
numeric aliases 1 and 2 are accepted.
.TP
.BI "--database " NAME
Select a database for hot backup or restore.
.TP
.BI "--backup-before-delete " YES|NO
Control cold backup before cluster deletion. The default is yes.
.TP
.BI "--clear-wal " YES|NO
Control emergency WAL reset before cold backup. The default is no.
.TP
.BI "--overwrite " YES|NO
Permit an existing user database to be dropped, recreated with its previous
owner, and restored from scratch. The default is no. The postgres, template0,
and template1 databases cannot be replaced.
.SH POSITIONAL TARGET
The
.B backup
and
.B delete
actions accept
.I VERSION CLUSTER
after the action, following the familiar
.B pg_ctlcluster
addressing style. Do not mix positional targeting with the corresponding named
options.
.SH BACKUPS
Cold archives contain configuration, data, the selected log file, systemd unit,
and metadata. Hot archives contain a custom-format dump and
.IR backup-info.env .
Before a cold backup, the data-directory size is displayed in the same aligned
nine-character format. Exact database and directory sizes in bytes are also
stored in metadata.
Hot metadata records database size and referenced application roles, including
available SCRAM or MD5 password verifiers. Missing roles are created before hot
restore; existing and system roles are not changed.
.PP
Each new metadata file starts with a commented, shell-escaped, non-interactive
.B create-claster-deb.sh
command. It rebuilds a mode 3 package from a cold archive or a mode 4 package
from a hot archive, recording the exact server package, cluster, port, absolute
backup path, hot database name, and a detectable custom data root.
.PP
When overwrite is enabled for an existing user database, the archive and dump
catalog are validated first. Active sessions are then terminated by
.BR "dropdb --force" ,
the complete database is recreated with its previous owner, and pg_restore runs
without object-by-object cleanup. This avoids failures on inherited constraints.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Command-line options override the corresponding variables:
.BR PGCC_ACTION ,
.BR PGCC_PACKAGE ,
.BR PGCC_PG_FAMILY ,
.BR PGCC_PG_VERSION ,
.BR PGCC_CLUSTER_NAME ,
.BR PGCC_CLUSTER_PORT ,
.BR PGCC_SCHEMA ,
.BR PGCC_DB_USER ,
.BR PGCC_DB_PASSWORD ,
.BR PGCC_DATA_ROOT ,
.BR PGCC_BACKUP_DIR ,
.BR PGCC_BACKUP_FILE ,
.BR PGCC_BACKUP_TYPE ,
.BR PGCC_DATABASE ,
.BR PGCC_BACKUP_BEFORE_DELETE ,
.BR PGCC_CLEAR_WAL ,
and
.BR PGCC_OVERWRITE .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/shared/pg_claster_creator/.new-claster.config
Preferred persistent defaults. Only if absent, the script uses
.I .new-claster.config
beside the resolved script, independently of the current working directory.
Saves update the selected file. This supports invocation through
.IR /usr/local/bin/create-claster.sh .
.TP
.I /.postgres
Service filesystem and default backup hierarchy.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/create-claster.sh
Installed command symlink.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo create-claster.sh
sudo create-claster.sh --action info
sudo create-claster.sh --action install --pg-version 16 \
  --cluster-name subsys --port 5432
sudo create-claster.sh --action backup 16 subsys \
  --backup-type hot --database asvd
sudo create-claster.sh --action restore \
  --backup-file /backup/16-asvd-20260905-105802-dmp.tar.gz \
  --pg-version 16 --cluster-name subsys --database asvd
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR create-claster-backup.sh (1),
.BR pg_lsclusters (1),
.BR pg_ctlcluster (1),
.BR pg_dump (1),
.BR pg_restore (1)
